  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung looks at his sons and then at Pear Blossom.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) The second son returns home.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and what now?\"",
  "[silence] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"We will sell out the east fields, father, and I will buy more land in the west fields where the land is better.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung feels the weight of his age.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and it is a good time for selling, for the land is fertile and the people are rich.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and what then?\"",
  "[action] The eldest son buys more land.",
  "the eldest son (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Well, and I will take the western fields and the eastern fields and the great fields that lie below the city wall, and I will buy more land in the south fields and there I will plant the flowers and the melons and the lotus flowers.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the second son): \"Now, and how will you pay for all this land?\"",
  "[says] Wang Lung expresses his inability to buy land.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"How should I buy it when I have not the money?\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung leaves the land",
